{
  "$comment": "Source spec for scripts/rocket/extract-sprites.js. Run with --spec scripts/coliseum/sheets.json: the pack name comes from this folder, so sources are read from frontend/src/assets/coliseum, PNGs export to frontend/public/coliseum, and review artefacts land in docs/images/coliseum/preview. Names are the texture keys the game asks for: armor is `${slot}-${group}` (group 0 = bronze, 1 = iron/steel, 2 = gold — see `armorGroup` in art.ts) and weapons/shields use their kind. RECIPE (learned 2026-09-12): the Stability models ignore long itemised briefs — asking for 28 pieces across 7 slots produced duplicate helmets, a fedora and a bucket, and a 9-weapon brief produced fantasy gems and staves. Asking for THREE pieces of ONE category produces exactly that, plus bonus filler rows below. So: one small single-category brief per sheet, then `exclude` the filler band. Prefer reading-order `names` (not `gridNames`) because the filler makes the layout irregular.",
  "defaults": {
    "pad": 12,
    "minSize": 26,
    "maxDim": 160,
    "$comment": "Icons are drawn at ~40px in the shop/inventory grids, so 160px is generous. Palette quantisation is what keeps a soft-shaded cartoon set in the low single-digit MB.",
    "png": {
      "compressionLevel": 9,
      "palette": true,
      "quality": 92,
      "effort": 8,
      "dither": 0.6
    }
  },
